  "releaseNotes": "## 12.1.5\n\n### Fixes\n- Pressing Enter inside a formatted list item now starts the next bullet in the same font, size, colour and decorations instead of reverting to the document default. Splitting a list item created the new item's paragraph without carrying the formatting active at the caret — unlike a non-list paragraph split — so a bullet typed in, say, Arial 12 produced a following bullet in the default font.\n- Structurally moving a block or paragraph that hosts an embedded control (`BlockUIContainer` or `RichInlineUIContainer`) — for example unwrapping a list item out of a list — no longer throws \"control already has a visual parent\". A moved element realizes a fresh render node, and the embedded control is now released from its previous node before the new one adopts it.",
